An interface method with `Self` nested in a composite param type (*[]Self, and
hence ...Self) is not satisfied by a correct impl: methodSigSatisfies /
substituteSelf should map *[]Self (Self=*Bag) to *[]*Bag and match the impl's
*[]*Bag, but the impl is rejected ("wrong signature").  Not variadic-specific (a
plain non-variadic *[]Self reproduces it); blocks a variadic ...Self interface /
constraint method.  Tracked in explorations/claude-todo.md.
